2026-11-04T01:36:08.6737552Z **What shipped (PR #1684, into `dev`)** — the single bounded, data-only change the handoff authorised:
2026-11-04T01:36:08.6738084Z 
2026-11-04T01:36:08.6741132Z - `…enclosed_left_annex.value.shoulder.front_gable_peak_m` **4.50 → 4.85 m**, so the small front-gable light over the enclosed shoulder reads as the sharply pointed cap Andreas's engraving draws instead of the blunt, nearly flat one (≈25.6° → ≈46.1° against the builder's unchanged 4.20 m head and 0.625 m half-span). Kept **reconstructed** — the plate has no scale, dimension, camera or date, and nothing is dated by it.
2026-11-04T01:36:08.6745259Z - Built on the pinned Blender 4.5.3, not hand-edited. `validate.py --stale` named exactly one stale master and exactly one was rebuilt: inputs `80d47de6a302 → bb16568756e3`, MASTER `0b53a6fe → f213818f`, WEB `0154cfad → 65863b3c`, derived in the same run. Every foreign registry row and producer family untouched.
2026-11-04T01:36:08.6748186Z - Exported-mesh comparison confines it: 3,318 → 3,330 triangles, two dormer ridge vertices up 0.35 m, 24 cladding vertices in the 4.307–4.581 m band, every other primitive byte-identical, **full bounding box exactly equal**.
2026-11-04T01:36:08.6751027Z - Controlled before/after through `photo_match.mjs` at the unchanged camera `9439f5f7` and picture `bfaa184f`; the previous side-by-side is preserved in `docs/RESEARCH/green-tree-annex-T-2376/`. The sharper cap is a real visible improvement, with no sky seam, hole or roof penetration.
2026-11-04T01:36:08.6755252Z - Match record stays **`differs`**: only the dormer cap is marked `fixed`, a new row stays **OPEN** for the shoulder's own roof slope and the left group's proportions. Trowbridge/Gale 1902's open bay, the unknown conversion date, the within-tolerance upper/attic count and camera residuals, and CHM c1859's unverified/link-only status are all preserved. Liberty entry, STATUS, research note and one What's-New entry appended, never replacing existing sections.
